{"lines": ["Back to Nyos. Here is what is known. The gas came out. A fountain of water and foam rose about a hundred metres, and a wave of at least twenty-five metres scoured one shore. The lake turned from blue to deep red.", "Here is what is not known. What triggered it.", "Most geologists suspect a landslide. Others suggest a small volcanic eruption on the lake bed, or cool rain overturning the water. An earthquake seems unlikely, because no tremors were reported.", "Nobody has proven which one it was.", "And at Roopkund, one question is still open. Why a group with Eastern Mediterranean ancestry was in the Himalayas around 1800. The study does not say.", "Rule five. Say what you don't know out loud. Saying it is not weakness. It is the only way the next person knows where to look."], "words": [["Back", 0.0, 0.14], ["to", 0.14, 0.34], ["Nyos.", 0.34, 0.92], ["Here", 0.92, 1.04], ["is", 1.04, 1.16], ["what", 1.16, 1.32], ["is", 1.32, 1.46], ["known.", 1.46, 1.66], ["The", 2.1, 2.15], ["gas", 2.15, 2.28], ["came", 2.28, 2.6], ["out.", 2.6, 2.9], ["A", 3.4, 3.45], ["fountain", 3.45, 3.7], ["of", 3.7, 3.94], ["water", 3.94, 4.2], ["and", 4.2, 4.42], ["foam", 4.42, 4.66], ["rose", 4.66, 5.0], ["about", 5.0, 5.32], ["a", 5.32, 5.647], ["hundred", 5.647, 5.973], ["metres,", 5.973, 6.3], ["and", 6.3, 6.58], ["a", 6.58, 6.68], ["wave", 6.68, 6.88], ["of", 6.88, 7.02], ["at", 7.02, 7.12], ["least", 7.12, 7.22], ["twenty-five", 7.22, 7.7], ["metres", 7.7, 8.18], ["scoured", 8.18, 8.64], ["one", 8.64, 8.88], ["shore.", 8.88, 9.2], ["The", 9.76, 9.81], ["lake", 9.81, 9.96], ["turned", 9.96, 10.26], ["from", 10.26, 10.54], ["blue", 10.54, 10.74], ["to", 10.74, 10.98], ["deep", 10.98, 11.16], ["red.", 11.16, 11.42], ["Here", 12.18, 12.54], ["is", 12.54, 12.72], ["what", 12.72, 12.92], ["is", 12.92, 13.06], ["not", 13.06, 13.26], ["known.", 13.26, 13.6], ["What", 13.88, 14.0], ["triggered", 14.0, 14.3], ["it.", 14.3, 14.58], ["Most", 15.42, 15.6], ["geologists", 15.6, 16.18], ["